rcent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nTested on v4.6.1.stable.official [14d19694e]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.1.stable - Fedora Linux 43 (KDE Plasma Desktop Edition) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 3 monitors - OpenGL 3 (Compatibility) - Mesa Intel(R) Iris(R) Xe Graphics (TGL GT2) - 11th Gen Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-11370H @ 3.30GHz (8 threads) - 62.52 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nSeems like a regression of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/100897 ?\n\nTrying to run the project with any fullscreen setting on Wayland, will result in the window not taking the fullscreen, unless it so happens that the project window resolution matches the screen resolution.\n\nTested on Compatibility and Mobile renderers.\n\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Go to `Project Settings > Display > Window > Mode` and set to `Exclusive Fullscreen` or `Fullscreen`\n2. Go to `Display > Display Server > Driver.linuxbsd` and set to `wayland`\n3. Run project. Window will run without decoration, but will not cover the whole screen if the screen resolution is higher than the project resolution.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"rsubtil","id":6501975,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY1MDE5NzU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6501975?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil","html_url":"https://github.com/rsubtil","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsubtil